    "explanation": "Both parties: the 5.00 SGD no-show fee on trip TRP-05051 stands, and under POL-NS-22 it is granted to the driver as compensation for time and fuel. The rider's request to waive it is not supported.\n\nWhy the fee stands. The driver's arrival at the pickup is established and corroborated. The platform trip record (EV-TRIP-05051, weight 1.0) logs the auto-arrival at 08:04:20, and the driver-device GPS trace (EV-GPS-05051, weight 1.0) confirms it: the nearest fix at 08:04:31 sits 3.74 m from the pickup point with a reported accuracy of 4 m, well inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, and the trace then holds stationary fixes continuously until 08:10:01. This is an on-demand trip with no scheduled time, so under POL-NS-21 the 300 s free wait ran from the driver's arrival at 08:04:20 and expired at 08:09:20. The driver cancelled at 08:10:05, 45 s after the wait expired: the wait was served, and the driver was entitled to cancel for a no-show.\n\nThe driver's contact obligation under POL-NS-23 is met. The chat log (EV-CHAT-05051, weight 1.0) shows in-app messages at 08:04:40 and 08:08:30, and the trip record shows an in-app call at 08:07:10 that rang 25 s unanswered. A message and a call both precede the 08:10:05 cancellation, so there is no basis to void the fee. The rider's own account supports this: she says she came down late, the driver's messages were read at 08:05:14 and 08:08:50, and her only reply came at 08:11:40, after the cancellation.\n\nThe rider's escalation argument (POL-GEN-26, POL-NS-26) is rejected. POL-GEN-26 applies where a fact a rule needs cannot be established because the evidence carrying it is missing or impaired. Every fact the no-show fee rule needs — the arrival, the free wait, the contact attempt, the cancellation and the fee — is carried by COMPLETE artifacts at weight 1.0. The only MISSING artifact is the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05051-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), which under POL-GEN-02(3) carries no fact and which no no-show rule turns on. The POL-NS-24 arrival deadline does not arise: the driver did arrive and waited, and it was the driver, not the rider, who cancelled, so there is no failure to arrive for that clause to reach and no open question to send to a reviewer. The rider's point that the 45 s margin is uncorroborated is also answered: the arrival is confirmed by both the platform record and the GPS trace, which agrees to 3.74 m.\n\nMoney and referrals. The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-05051, weight 1.0) shows exactly 5.00 SGD charged, matching the policy fee, with nothing refunded, and POL-NS-22 directs that where the fee stands the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION with amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both equal to the fee charged. No referral fires: the POL-NS-25 repeat no-show counter (rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d) is absent from the rider's profile, so that referral cannot be raised; the fee charged is exactly the 5.00 SGD the policy fixes, so POL-NS-22's fee-amount check adds nothing; and the POL-NS-24 goodwill credit does not apply because the driver both messaged and called.\n\nConfidence 0.95, against a cap of 1.0 — the lowest weight among the artifacts carrying the deciding facts, all of which are 1.0 — and a required confidence of 0.0, since the dispute is below 10.00 SGD with no fraud flag on either profile (POL-GEN-22, POL-NS-26)."
